#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bfd9fab-eee2-5452-9cef-7e428deaaf4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-4{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310843} {:answer/id #uuid "a5162f30-f9f8-56f0-87e3-c050745c20d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310844} {:answer/id #uuid "72905702-3042-5474-a8ed-03080ecbc5a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-2x}+C{x}^{2}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310845} {:answer/id #uuid "1547bd12-2561-5d09-8e55-3a2f8e1e5a46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+Dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310846} {:answer/id #uuid "20516aab-1dff-53db-99bc-d2fc0df33732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+C{e}^{-x}+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5162f30-f9f8-56f0-87e3-c050745c20d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310844} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc0e6c8d-b9b0-5a01-9ad3-7b6d7b3d5bd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "795b711d-ea65-5cb8-87a2-70f0c9e6f190" :question/math-academy-id "q-119038" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=8{e}^{-2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\int {e}^{-2x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+C \\\\  & =-4{e}^{-2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{-2x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec6175a2-7628-54e2-9a83-5ea329ef75ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^2-\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec6175a2-7628-54e2-9a83-5ea329ef75ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^2-\\frac{25}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335544} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc032f3-fbc1-54cb-8244-03c727fb366d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85b460c5-45ef-565d-85f6-70fe7fc6f047" :question/math-academy-id "q-347842" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $8x-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=5.$\n\n$y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,+${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}+8x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-{x}^{2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+4({2}^{2})+C \\\\ 5 & =-\\frac{8}{3}+16+C \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{40}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+4{x}^{2}-\\frac{25}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4ab07a7-d1ed-5f44-8915-09e7b2418825" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of a Differential Equation With a Given Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c37723-0d69-5949-9392-9e4a22784beb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6{x}^{3}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335547} {:answer/id #uuid "f662054e-567a-5206-baa6-0c106c3270f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335548} {:answer/id #uuid "8506772a-2ec6-5eb3-a530-4e04ad831e12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2{x}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335549} {:answer/id #uuid "a9fb4249-c501-5987-bf77-623752e67114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3{x}^{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335550} {:answer/id #uuid "c99f4f6a-afd7-5903-ab46-48898f42996a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c99f4f6a-afd7-5903-ab46-48898f42996a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{x}^{3}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335551} :answer-field/id #uuid "0367d76d-393f-563b-8a18-a5ef095afd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1eb154da-4739-51ad-b420-cb4dc79403e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-50044" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=2$\n \n\n$$\nx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{3}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=2{x}^{3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(-1)=2$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =2(-1)^{3}+C \\\\ 2 & =-2+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nf(x)=2{x}^{3}+4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a745d53-2adc-5935-a97d-5a586599fa37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095684} {:answer/id #uuid "f4387418-5075-52c7-b685-924f2791a4be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095685} {:answer/id #uuid "035eddbc-75fb-53ba-bc61-c5e0c4f3f025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095686} {:answer/id #uuid "12887777-c8a6-5e16-bf30-ed290559c1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-\\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx^{2} + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095687} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68fbfe-8f1c-512a-8cc2-1b00fe18af49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{3}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "035eddbc-75fb-53ba-bc61-c5e0c4f3f025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = \\frac{1}{9}e^{3x} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095686} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5a4615-20d2-563a-8738-3f3905aa1549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e04bc45-f34f-56fc-9a0e-8643597c4852" :question/math-academy-id "q-50148" :question/problem "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{e}^{3x}=0.\n$$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,{e}^{3x})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3x}+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335552 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23789a74-f1e3-5e26-8678-21f84a11a12b" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Solution Curves of a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce5a1a22-4b15-5473-b750-1020ede68b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/ff60bb4fceb52346f5f9b4275343729a737dd52e0283beaaeb4d740e1751feca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335554} {:answer/id #uuid "38afabcd-d507-5b5e-83a5-9dec681cd7cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/09fb3125c260d2f042ec3a509bb7e776d0d47ece3e78255931f8bc9781aa31c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335555} {:answer/id #uuid "50b3afae-2b5a-5d32-9f05-62decfb8aa63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/af10bb7e5a91561be6d83950803920c8c74aeee40f7982c0564250f707628cbb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335556} {:answer/id #uuid "bd8980fd-0ff7-5beb-bc78-02a616ebdf40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/9908bd23538332705791bbd968dfdf5e22ddde8884aaa9fed58268bc1132d208.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335557} {:answer/id #uuid "2d89dbb7-8700-51aa-a90e-9804c52e79c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/8ca894c5a5ca9e93af8c39242ba1584447472bb81c872e1225c52a4fbc652e1c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50b3afae-2b5a-5d32-9f05-62decfb8aa63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/af10bb7e5a91561be6d83950803920c8c74aeee40f7982c0564250f707628cbb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335556} :answer-field/id #uuid "10e6a4ef-c119-5032-a4c4-9df0295af8c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7716424-9b11-538f-a06b-55bd73654360" :question/math-academy-id "q-79565" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/fa13b048e5ca54c7074bbf6ec11421bfd8fb9e1618abd732a5faa1d78372a863.png)"}]}
